{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1096739-can-intimidation-work-too-well-like-unleashings","id":1096739,"title":"Can Intimidation work too Well like Unleashings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-25T08:39:24-07:00","id":1096739,"title":"Can Intimidation work too Well like Unleashings?","content":"One thing about Intimidation, is you want someone to do something usualy, not simply to collapse in terror.<br /> <br /> Is it possible for Intimidation too work too well? Say a garou snarls at a pentex employee &quot;Open the safe!&quot; or a parent snaps their belt at a child &quot;Clean your room&quot; and rolls 4 or 5 succeses<br /> Hopefully, those who've studied Machiavelli, as I have, keep that in mind.<br /> But can too successful attempts to frighten someone render them too blank to even obey your commands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T09:52:03-07:00","id":1096779,"title":"","content":"Sort of, but that 's not &quot;working too well&quot;. The target counterproductively freaking out could well be the result of a botch, though, in appropriate circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T16:19:46-07:00","id":1096896,"title":"","content":"From a purely game design perspective: No. It's dumb to punish players because they have a character that's good/lucky at something by making it less effective. If a character can regularly get 4-5 successes on Intimidation rolls, they're good enough that they're not screwing up future attempts.<br /> <br /> From a more &quot;realism&quot; focused perspective, the problem is that Intimidation generally covers two very different psychological mechanisms (though two that are frequently used in combination). The &quot;blank out and freeze&quot; is usually a result of failing to dance the line between those techniques, or because the individual is already in a state of mental shock. In other words, either someone screws up Intimidation, or social actions are pretty much lost on the target in the first place.<br /> <br /> I feel that part of the problem is that well executed Intimidation rarely looks like overt threats. When a police officer starts barking orders, they've already felt they've intimidated an individual into compliance via the threat of authority and force. If you listen to police, they don't threaten, they order. Adding, &quot;...or I'll shoot!&quot; after an order means they haven't already intimidated the subject. We perceive the orders as intimidation, instead of the uniform, the societal teaching of respect/fear of authority, being armed, and similar tools used to instill compliance before a word is said. You see the same thing in cults. Cults spend a lot of time doing things that are seen as friendly gestures to potential members, but are actually setting them up for later intimidation should they try to leave or question the cult's leadership. &quot;Let's go on a camping trip,&quot; doesn't sound like intimidation, but it can be part of isolation tactics to make a target feel like the cult is the only home they have, and feel like anything that risks them being forced out is too scary to consider.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T17:44:21-07:00","id":1096916,"title":"","content":"No, but if a Garou has too high a Rage, they have to use it instead of Charisma + Intimidation during facedowns, and if they get too many successes, they freak out counterproductively (and frenzy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T18:16:45-07:00","id":1096935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1096739-can-intimidation-work-too-well-like-unleashings?p=1096896#post1096896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a purely game design perspective: No. It's dumb to punish players because they have a character that's good/lucky at something by making it less effective. If a character can regularly get 4-5 successes on Intimidation rolls, they're good enough that they're not screwing up future attempts.<br /> <br /> From a more &quot;realism&quot; focused perspective, the problem is that Intimidation generally covers two very different psychological mechanisms (though two that are frequently used in combination). The &quot;blank out and freeze&quot; is usually a result of failing to dance the line between those techniques, or because the individual is already in a state of mental shock. In other words, either someone screws up Intimidation, or social actions are pretty much lost on the target in the first place.<br /> <br /> I feel that part of the problem is that well executed Intimidation rarely looks like overt threats. When a police officer starts barking orders, they've already felt they've intimidated an individual into compliance via the threat of authority and force. If you listen to police, they don't threaten, they order. Adding, &quot;...or I'll shoot!&quot; after an order means they haven't already intimidated the subject. We perceive the orders as intimidation, instead of the uniform, the societal teaching of respect/fear of authority, being armed, and similar tools used to instill compliance before a word is said. You see the same thing in cults. Cults spend a lot of time doing things that are seen as friendly gestures to potential members, but are actually setting them up for later intimidation should they try to leave or question the cult's leadership. &quot;Let's go on a camping trip,&quot; doesn't sound like intimidation, but it can be part of isolation tactics to make a target feel like the cult is the only home they have, and feel like anything that risks them being forced out is too scary to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much this. The game has some fundimental &quot;Gamey&quot; bits and not punishing players for rolling well is probably out there. I mean one could just as readily make arguments on &quot;rolling really well&quot; On seduction attempts give you an auto stalker or that damage should always be hidden from the player so they don't know how much they've taken or how much they've given out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T09:48:35-07:00","id":1099193,"title":"","content":"oh curious on the telling a Pentex employee to open a safe? Ideas how to mark it as more or less successful? since if he's just an ordinary employee intimidating him may only be so difficult?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T18:37:40-07:00","id":1099707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1096739-can-intimidation-work-too-well-like-unleashings?p=1099193#post1099193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious on the telling a Pentex employee to open a safe? Ideas how to mark it as more or less successful? since if he's just an ordinary employee intimidating him may only be so difficult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Go too low on the hierarchy, and your intimidation attempts to coerce the employee might be like getting blood from a stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T06:43:18-07:00","id":1099806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1096739-can-intimidation-work-too-well-like-unleashings?p=1099707#post1099707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Go too low on the hierarchy, and your intimidation attempts to coerce the employee might be like getting blood from a stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point...<br /> <br /> But at whatever point on the hierchy, ideas on how to make intimidation more or less successful based on the number of successes?<br /> <br /> One Idea I have?<br /> <br /> is with enough successes hes unable to plot while being threatened, dutifully obeying the Garou And may miss opportunitys to turn the tables on them? <br /> <br /> Another is that he may be slower to report things after the fact if they get more successes as he'll have a lingering terror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}